<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Minimal stand-in for a `vcover report -xml -details -cvg` export, used by
     bin/tests/test_converters.py.

     Questa writes each covergroup *type* of a package as a flat sequence of
     siblings under the package's <instanceData>: the summary <bin> naming the
     type, its <type_option>, the type-level <coverpoint>/<cross> summaries
     (which report only a percentage and three bin counts, and whose <bins> is
     always empty), and then one <coverinstance> per instantiated copy. Only the
     instances name the bins and say how often each was hit, so they are what the
     UCIS converter reads; the summaries above it are kept here to prove it
     ignores them.

     Shaped to cover every path the converter takes: bins that were hit and bins
     that were not, an ignore and an illegal bin, a coverpoint with no bins at all
     (unrepresentable in UCIS), a cross naming it (so that cross has to go), a cross
     naming its bins by the pair they combine (so they are written), a cross bin
     over a * bin of a crossed coverpoint and a cross-level ignore bin (neither
     names one combination, so both have to go), and a package with no bins anywhere
     (so that instance has to go).

     Shapes taken from the real export it stands in for, so the tests are not testing
     an invention: Questa crosses two or more coverpoints (never one, and this file
     keeps one anyway to pin that path), it names a cross bin by the tuple of the
     crossed bins in the order the coverpoints are crossed, it writes no <bin_rhs>
     under a counted cross bin but does under an ignore bin of the cross, and the
     tuple of a cross bin of this export is never a bare "<*>".

     __REPO__ is replaced with the repository root by the test. -->
